Root cause:
The bug was caused by the integration of archive extraction into the attachment saving process, which inadvertently led to a situation where both `save_self` and `save_extracted` could be false, preventing any save tasks from being executed and breaking the "Open with" functionality.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (!attachment->priv->save_self && !attachment->priv->save_extracted)
```
```c
if (attachment->priv->save_self)
```
```c
if (attachment->priv->save_extracted)
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the condition checks if both `save_self` and `save_extracted` are false, which prevents any save tasks from being executed. This results in the "Open with" functionality being broken, as no saving operation can proceed if both flags are false.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!attachment->priv->save_self && !attachment->priv->save_extracted)
    attachment->priv->save_self = TRUE;
```
Reason:
This code ensures that if both `save_self` and `save_extracted` are false, it sets `save_self` to true, thereby allowing at least one save task to be executed. This change restores the functionality needed for the "Open with" feature to work correctly.


